  "colorScheme": {
    "$note": "A scheme overrides exactly these ten roles on top of the active theme: accent, accent2, accentSoft, onAccent, the brand gradient (g1→g2), page, pageWarm, pageCool, app, app2. It must never change semantic status colors (good/warn/crit/info) or the fixed category hues, because a user learns those meanings once. Night theme keeps only accent and accent2 from the scheme and supplies its own grounds. NibbleCue’s default is leaf, a fresh green built from CuddleCue’s solids hue (2026-10-08, the owner: the main color tells the two apps apart, and solids is green in CuddleCue; leaf takes Sunny’s place in the six); CuddleCue’s default is ocean, a clear blue (the owner, 2026-09-27: the green default felt boring and should be a brighter color); it is the one scheme the free plan paints, and an unknown key falls back to it. Reef, the logo’s teal and coral, was the default from 2026-09-21 and stays as a choice. A retired key is never reused for different hues: twilight (retired 2026-09-21), and sage and clay (retired 2026-09-27, replaced by lilac and sunny), fall back to the default wherever a device or a profile row still holds one. Stored per user on profiles.color_scheme. Gradient labels use onGradient (always #FFFFFF), never onAccent: onAccent is correct on the flat accent, but the gradient's light end needs white. Every g1 is tuned so white text clears 4.5:1 on it.",
    "$default": "leaf",
