  "moduleDisc": {
    "$note": "THE OWNER'S COLOR REFERENCE (2026-09-22): the swatches, and which module wears each. These are FILL colors and never ink — measured, every one fails as text on white (1.2-2.8:1) while the brand ink ON them clears 4.8-11.1:1, which is what a disc behind a dark glyph wants. So they paint the circle at FULL STRENGTH — a holder that composited them toward the ground was the reason the sheet kept not showing up on the phone — and `categoryColorByModule` keeps naming the ink token that paints a line, a label or a chart series.",
    "$night": "Night mode does not use these. The amber screen exists to keep a dark room dark, and seven saturated discs are the one thing it is for; night keeps its own dimmed category colors.",
    "swatch": {
      "feed": "#FFD166",
      "breastfeed": "#E87C8E",
      "pump": "#A7E3C1",
      "diaper": "#FFB3A7",
      "sleep": "#C7B4EB",
      "tummy": "#A7DBFF",
      "solids": "#BDE3A7",
      "health": "#FFB3CB",
      "bath": "#D9F5A1",
      "med": "#D2A1F5"
    },
    "byModule": {
