    "$eighth": "Breastfeeding is the eighth, added 2026-09-22: it no longer shares the bottle's amber. It is the only swatch that is not a pastel (0.335 relative luminance against the others' 0.58-0.83), which is what keeps it apart from `health` nine degrees away on the wheel — 1.6:1 of lightness between them. Bath and medicine are DERIVED, not on the owner's sheet: built at the mean saturation and lightness of the reference (0.80/0.795) at the hue each module's ink already uses, because leaving them on someone else's put two identical cells in Today's care strip."
